  "notes": "USAGE: {召|め}す is an honorific (sonkeigo) verb with several meanings depending on context. The most common modern uses are お{召|め}し{上|あ}がる (to eat/drink, honorific) and お{召|め}しになる (to wear, honorific).\n\nThe \"summon\" meaning is mostly used in historical or formal contexts.\n\nASPECT (ている): お{召|め}しになっている describes the state of wearing something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- お{召|め}し{上|あ}がる: to eat/drink (honorific compound)\n- お{召|め}しになる: to wear (honorific form)\n- お{召|め}し{物|もの}: clothing (honorific)\n- [food/drink]を{召|め}し{上|あ}がる (to eat/drink something)\n- [clothing]をお{召|め}しになる (to wear something)\n- [person]を{召|め}す (to summon someone)",
